Move one endpoint of an existing edge to a different node, keeping the
edge row (id, sentence, evidence linkage, provenance) intact. The drain
op for Disambiguation attachment points: once the true referent of an
attached edge is determined, re-point it from the Disambiguation node
to the referent.

Audited: requires a non-empty `reason`; refuses user-locked edges and
edges whose old or new endpoint nodes are user-locked; refuses
self-loops and re-points that would duplicate an existing edge;
snapshots before/after into kg_revision_log so the change can be
reverted. Pass `dry_run: true` to preview without committing.
